      "description": "Workforce and Continuing Education - Wilmington College (Wilmington, Ohio) Liberal Arts College Skip to Main Content Apply Visit Request Info Give Athletics WC HUB WC HUB and quick links WILLPAY LOGIN View your bill, make payments, and manage your student account. WC Portal Find your schedules, grades, and campus announcements in one place. Menu Utility Navigation Apply Visit Request Info Give Athletics WC HUB WILLPAY LOGIN WC Portal Workforce and Continuing Education Home Workforce and Continuing Education Workforce and Continuing Education Learn. Grow. Lead Explore how we can help you level up. Our broad selection of seminars, training courses, and credentials is designed to help you and your team stay current on important industry and workplace needs, as well as improve operations across your organization. Many of our training options can be offered on-site, on-campus, or online. Some options are designed for multiple sessions or days, but may be tailored depending on your needs. At Wilmington College, our Quaker values guide how we approach both work and learning – providing hands-on opportunities for career and professional development. We’ll help you make a lasting difference and build your purpose wherever you are. Workforce Training Whether you’re looking to grow in your current field, or change careers, or if you’re just getting started, you’ll work with people who've been in your shoes and know how to get to where you want to go. Learn more Credentials and Certifications Our broad selection of seminars and trainings are designed to help you and your staff stay current on important industry and workplace needs, as well improving operations across your organization. learn more Continuing Education From CEUs to adding a micro credential or a certification, go further in your career or earn credit toward a degree program with the Continuing Education program at Wilmington College. Learn more , Connect Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Wilmington College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation or disability in the administration of educational policies, admission policies, financial aid, employment or any other College program or activity. Disclosures © 2026 Wilmington College. All rights reserved"
