    "https://www.wilmington.edu/career-services": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services - Wilmington College (Wilmington, Ohio) Liberal Arts College Skip to Main Content Apply Visit Request Info Give Athletics WC HUB WC HUB and quick links WILLPAY LOGIN View your bill, make payments, and manage your student account. WC Portal Find your schedules, grades, and campus announcements in one place. Menu Utility Navigation Apply Visit Request Info Give Athletics WC HUB WILLPAY LOGIN WC Portal Career Services The Office of Career Services is here to help you! The career acceleration tools and platforms offered to students by career services prepare them for the professional world by providing them with internship opportunities, resume building, interview tips and the ability to begin networking. Step into your future by scheduling a career advising appointment today, to map out your success and start networking with top employers! Schedule an appointment Home Career Services Time to Register for our Annual Career & Grad Fair! Looking to discover what's next in your educational career? Connect and network with future employers at Wilmington College's Annual Career & Grad School Fair on October 29th, 2026! All Wilmington College students are welcome to attend and explore various career opportunities. Registration for students will open September 1, 2026. Student registration Handshake Career Services at Wilmington College is proud to partner with Handshake. Handshake is the online platform Wilmington College provides for a variety of career development-related activities including student professional profiles, career-related events, and employer engagement. This platform is used by hundreds of colleges and universities, and thousands of employers. All students are provided access to Handshake when they enroll at Wilmington College. LOGIN TO HANDSHAKE Focus 2 A comprehensive career planning platform providing work interest, values, personality, and skills assessments to help guide you in making the most of your time here. Linking to Wilmington College majors and Bureau of Labor Statistics career field growth projections through 2034, FOCUS II can help you plan for the fulfilling professional future you want. LOGIN TO FOCUS 2 VMock This AI-powered career acceleration platform, a partner of Wilmington College, offers tools designed to help students improve their resumes, LinkedIn profiles, and interview skills. Vmock uses Artificial Intelligence and data analytics from across the web to help users score, revise, and improve their career documents, optimizing potential outcomes in the job market. LOGIN TO VMOCK Internships Internships are an integral part of your college experience – complementing your academic program and providing the experience you need to prepare for the career you want. Completing internships can give you a competitive advantage in the job market for college graduates. Student Employment & Work Study Wilmington College offers numerous opportunities for students to work on campus through Federal Work Study (part of your financial aid), and non-Federal Work Study positions.You can access On-Campus Job Listings here. Career and Professional Development Making connections between the work you are doing in your classes to career opportunities beyond the classroom, we strive to connect you in diverse and personalized ways with the people, organizations, skills, and opportunities to make your unique vision a reality. College and Career Academy Designed for grades 9-12, get a jump start on college and earn up to 4 academic credits. Employer Job Posting on Handshake To post jobs on Handshake , please log in to your account HERE , or create a Handshake account HERE .  For additional information or help getting started with Handshake, please email suzanne.harmon@wilmington.edu . Want more info? Loading Loading , Connect Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Wilmington College does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation or disability in the administration of educational policies, admission policies, financial aid, employment or any other College program or activity. Disclosures © 2026 Wilmington College. All rights reserved"
